1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
AquaShift: a working water-planning demo
Historical weather, scenario demand and tariffs; operator advice only.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Grid: produce equal water at a different time
2,880 m³ and 9,792 kWh in both schedules; cost change comes from clock prices.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Change the tank: the schedule responds
A 500 m³ tank reduces flexibility; the modeled supply and safety constraints still hold.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Evaluation: test the model against a fair simple method
The reference loses on average error: 8.8 vs 7.6 W/m². AI benefit remains unproven.

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Inspect actual, model and simple prediction
Real historical reconstruction; solar radiation is a weather proxy, not measured grid surplus.

6
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Sites: irrigation budget and injected leak
Four synthetic leak hours detected. Meter data is simulated; field accuracy is untested.

7
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
A reproducible prototype with a clear next pilot
Reference model replaceable by Stefanos; site data, real tariffs and operating limits are next.
